b.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3069153958,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6275Km","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T11:35:56Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T11:36:14Z","body":"> only concerning itself with the thing we already know is a file path\r\n\r\nDoes this also work for `print_debug()`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3069153958/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3069183402","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108473#issuecomment-3069183402","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3069183402,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc628AWq","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T11:46:45Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T11:46:45Z","body":"> Does this also work for `print_debug()`?\r\n\r\nNo. Those paths are not added (or otherwise parsed) in `EditorLog`, so would require parsing of the log messages. Same goes for `print_stack()`.\r\n\r\nI'd prefer to keep this PR limited to errors/warnings, since that's what the two proposals are about.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3069183402/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3118607651","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108473#issuecomment-3118607651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3118607651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc654i0j","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T15:25:36Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T15:33:46Z","body":"> which means only `@tool` scripts will benefit from this change\r\n\r\nThe main motivation for this was being able to click the paths of GDScript parse errors, where this also applies.\r\n\r\n> errors/warnings printed in the running project appear in the **Debugger > Errors** tab instead\r\n\r\nIndeed, and those are clickable already.\r\n\r\n> Also, links to C++ source files will appear to be clickable, but will do nothing when clicked.\r\n\r\nYes, that would be the \"potentially controversial change\" mentioned in the PR description.\r\n\r\nI was toying with the idea of maybe being able to open up GitHub links to the actual file and line for C++ errors, since we should have the commit and everything, but that probably gets messy very quickly, especially when you start involving custom forks, custom modules and godot-cpp errors and whatever else there might be.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3118607651/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3121529013","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108473#issuecomment-3121529013","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3121529013,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66DsC1","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-26T08:54:18Z","updated_at":"2025-07-26T08:54:18Z","body":"I forgot to escape `[` in the other `err_str` case. Should be fixed now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3121529013/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141205104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108473#issuecomment-3141205104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3141205104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67Ovxw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T20:09:34Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T20:09:34Z","body":"> C++ will include relative file paths (e.g. editor/editor_log.cpp:201) which I couldn't see an easy way to deal with, and forwarding those to OS::shell_open will typically open the user's browser at that (bogus) path, so I opted to have it do nothing instead.\r\n\r\n`shell_open()` will open the file in default program. You could check if the file exists before making it clickable. Opening cpp files is useful for custom builds.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141205104/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141459229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108473#issuecomment-3141459229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3141459229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67Pt0d","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T22:00:47Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T22:01:34Z","body":"> You could check if the file exists before making it clickable. Opening cpp files is useful for custom builds.\r\n\r\nBy \"before making it clickable\" do you mean adding not adding `[url]` to it if it fails the `file_exists` check? Adding I/O (or even syscalls in general) to every logged message seems questionable, even if we're talking about error messages.\r\n\r\nIf you mean only having it passed to `shell_open` in `_meta_clicked` if it passes `file_exist` there, then sure. They likely wouldn't be absolute paths though, and assuming that the working directory is the root of the source tree seems questionable as well. I've had mine set to either `bin` or the project directory for years now, just to give one example.\r\n\r\nI suppose it's easy enough to make the URI scheme optional in the `_meta_clicked` regex and prepend `OS::_execpath` and `..` and test for that path instead. You wouldn't be able to make use of the line number with `shell_open` though, I assume.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141459229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144302820","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108473#issuecomment-3144302820","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3144302820,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67akDk","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T11:49:17Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T11:50:08Z","body":"> By \"before making it clickable\" do you mean adding not adding [url] to it if it fails the file_exists check? Adding I/O (or even syscalls in general) to every logged message seems questionable, even if we're talking about error messages.\r\n\r\nIt would only affect messages with file paths. Would it be that expensive? 🤔 For repeating errors it could be cached and the cache can be cleared when clearing output.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144302820/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144332875","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108473#issuecomment-3144332875","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108473","id":3144332875,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67arZL","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T11:59:55Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T11:59:55Z","body":"> For repeating errors it could be cached and the cache can be cleared when clearing output.\r\n\r\nIs it really worth the trouble though? I don't find it particularly strange that they're underlined/clickable without anything happening when you click it.\r\n\r\nEither way, I'd prefer if that was done in a follow-up PR, assuming it's not deemed a blocker for this one.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144332875/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192357222","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/god